Z||000000||sloth85GT||10-07-2001||12:46 PM||||This was like the third one, I didn't bother with the guy until he started pulling cool daddy G on me driving right beside me speeding up then slowing down, then pulling up then slowing down. Then at a red light he squeaked his tires as best he can and sped down Portage. So I thought "this little punk is gonna see how slow his car really is". Next stop light I hit it. When I hit about 70, he was 2 car lengths behind me. And I know he was trying cause I heard that little chirp from his tires. Needless to say, he didn't try anything else until I turned off on Inkster to head home.<P>I don't like those young punks that think they can race a slow car. I ran into the same thing in the beginning of the summer with these two 16 or 17 year old in daddy's Neon. They were revving the engine beside me and I yell out to them, "I'll give you 3 car lengths". And I did. I caught them and of course they were like "holy ****  man, what do you have in there?". Nobody knows that it's a V6. Just a plain ol stock V6. Same response I got from killing a Cavalier Z24. I think that's enough for now, just want to end by saying that I love my Fiero.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">     <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT||||reg||10
